DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The function cclleeaarreerrrr() clears the end‐of‐file and error indicators for
       the stream pointed to by _s_t_r_e_a_m.

       The  function  ffeeooff()  tests  the  end‐of‐file indicator for the stream
       pointed to by _s_t_r_e_a_m, returning nonzero if it is set.  The  end‐of‐file
       indicator can be cleared only by the function cclleeaarreerrrr().

       The  function ffeerrrroorr() tests the error indicator for the stream pointed
       to by _s_t_r_e_a_m, returning nonzero if it is set.  The error indicator  can
       be reset only by the cclleeaarreerrrr() function.

       For nonlocking counterparts, see uunnlloocckkeedd__ssttddiioo(3).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The ffeeooff() function returns nonzero if the end‐of‐file indicator is set
       for _s_t_r_e_a_m; otherwise, it returns zero.

       The ffeerrrroorr() function returns nonzero if the error indicator is set for
       _s_t_r_e_a_m; otherwise, it returns zero.

EERRRROORRSS
       These functions should not fail and do not set _e_r_r_n_o.

