       POSIX.1‐2008 specifies that these functions shall not change the value
       of _e_r_r_n_o if _s_t_r_e_a_m is valid.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
       Normally, programs should read the return value of an input function,
       such as ffggeettcc(3), before using functions of the ffeeooff(3) family.  Only
       when the function returned the sentinel value EEOOFF it makes sense to
       distinguish between the end of a file or an error with ffeeooff(3) or
       ffeerrrroorr(3).

